        "original_id": "4cdb0d57-d006-5c1a-9097-d4da107fc2d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michaël Llodra, Juan Martín del Potro, Novak Djokovic, Tomáš Berdych, Robin Söderling, Jo-Wilfried Tsonga, Nikolay Davydenko, Janko Tipsarević, John Isner, Gaël Monfils\n- Events: 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament – Singles\n- Organizations: Association of Tennis Professionals\n- Concepts: doubles success, singles titles, world rankings\n\nFacts:\n- Juan Martín del Potro was born on 23 September 1988 and is an Argentinian professional tennis player.\n- Juan Martín del Potro has also been known by the nickname Delpo.\n- Juan Martín del Potro was ranked world No. 24 in men's singles by the Association of Tennis Professionals.\n- Michaël Llodra won three Grand Slam championships in doubles and an Olympic silver medal.\n- Michaël Llodra won five career singles titles.\n- Michaël Llodra recorded singles victories over Novak Djokovic, Juan Martín del Potro, Tomáš Berdych, Robin Söderling, Jo-Wilfried Tsonga, Nikolay Davydenko, Janko Tipsarević, and John Isner.\n- Michaël Llodra was the defending champion at the 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament – Singles.\n- Michaël Llodra lost in the second round of the 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament – Singles to Gaël Monfils.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
